# Avatar 59 fps base with frame generation x2 (118 fps displayed on a VRR panel), declared -src 60, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. All nine benchmark tests, every inter-test fade kept (frame generation stops on a fade, so the source drops 118 to 59 and the batches go from pairs to singletons), desktop trimmed off both ends.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 59 fps base with frame generation x2 (118 fps displayed on a VRR panel), declared -src 60, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. All nine benchmark tests, every inter-test fade kept (frame generation stops on a fade, so the source drops 118 to 59 and the batches go from pairs to singletons), desktop trimmed off both ends.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 39
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 45.1
# Replay 44.6% / runs 0 / worst 43 against field 45.1% / runs 0 / worst 39. The model runs
# slightly long on the worst run and slightly short on the share, both by margins the fades
# explain: frame generation STOPS on a fade, so the batches collapse from pairs to singletons
# mid-window and the arrival geometry changes under the policy rather than around it. That
# transition is the reason to keep the fades in this one.
max_worst_run 43
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 45.0
min_reseeds 3
